400 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (This report assesses the alignment of financial incentives within India's dairy sector with the principles of animal welfare, environmental sustainability, and public health. While extensive financial support is leading to the sector's growth, the analysis carried out demonstrates a concerning tendency for incentives to prioritize economic gains at the expense of sustainable practices. Consequently, the report highlights the persistence of issues such as poor animal welfare, environmental degradation, and potential risks to public health and food safety.   )
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1 2]
>>
endobj
401 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (The report recommends restructuring of financial incentives to leverage them as drivers for positive change. It proposes that access to funding be linked to verifiable improvements in key areas, including animal husbandry practices, effective pollution control, and the adoption of sustainable farming methods. To achieve this transformation, the report calls for strengthened accountability and monitoring mechanisms within the financial support system, ensuring that the pursuit of economic growth in the dairy sector is effectively balanced with responsibility towards animal well-being, environmental preservation, and public health.)
/Pg 9 0 R
>>
endobj
