/P 1417 0 R
/T (Siting Policy - The establishment should be located at least 200 meters away from residential dwellings and 500 meters away from hospitals and schools. It must not be situated in flood-prone areas that are subject to flooding at a frequency of 1-in-25 years or more, to prevent contamination of water bodies. Locations with shallow groundwater depths of around 10 to 12 feet, especially in alluvium areas, should be avoided to prevent groundwater contamination. The site should also maintain a minimum distance of 200 meters from National Highways and 100 meters from State Highways. Additionally, it must be at least 500 meters away from major drinking water reservoirs on the catchment side, 100 meters from drinking water sources such as wells, summer storage tanks, and other tanks, 500 meters from major watercourses like rivers and lakes, and 200 meters from canals. An inter-se distance of at least 5 meters should be maintained between two establishments to allow for adequate ventilation. Each unit must also provide a setback of at least 2.5 meters on each side and develop a green belt around the facility.)
/E (Siting Policy - The establishment should be located at least 200 meters away from residential dwellings and 500 meters away from hospitals and schools. It must not be situated in flood-prone areas that are subject to flooding at a frequency of 1-in-25 years or more, to prevent contamination of water bodies. Locations with shallow groundwater depths of around 10 to 12 feet, especially in alluvium areas, should be avoided to prevent groundwater contamination. The site should also maintain a minimum distance of 200 meters from National Highways and 100 meters from State Highways. Additionally, it must be at least 500 meters away from major drinking water reservoirs on the catchment side, 100 meters from drinking water sources such as wells, summer storage tanks, and other tanks, 500 meters from major watercourses like rivers and lakes, and 200 meters from canals. An inter-se distance of at least 5 meters should be maintained between two establishments to allow for adequate ventilation. Each unit must also provide a setback of at least 2.5 meters on each side and develop a green belt around the facility.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [1]
>>
