/E (State/municipal statutes generally empower local bodies to inspect milch cattle and regulate the infrastructure \(aspects such as construction, dimensions\), ventilation, lighting, cleansing-drainage, and water supply of dairies and cattle sheds. The local bodies are also authorized to regulate dairies, cattle sheds, milk shops, and stores, and to issue licenses for dairy operations, depending on the concerned area. Additionally, local bodies have the mandate to establish cattle pounds, levy penalties for allowing cattle to stray on streets or trespass on private or public property, and impose fines or seize animals found abandoned, roaming, or tethered in public spaces. They are also responsible for preventing the tethering of animals and the milking of cattle on public streets. Accordingly, every dairy owner is required to obtain a license or no-objection certificate \(NOC\) from the local body.)
/Pg 19 0 R
/K [1]
>>
