/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (2. Flooring: Proper flooring is essential for maintaining hygiene and preventing injuries and disease in dairy cattle. The Central Pollution Control Board \(CPCB\) guidelines mandate that floors in dairy housing should be impervious, non-slippery, and equipped with a wastewater collection system. Inadequate flooring such as damp, uneven, or abrasive surfaces can lead to respiratory illness in calves and significantly increase the risk of lameness in adult cattle. In India, lameness affects an estimated 8% to 30.5% of dairy cattle and is widely recognised as the most reliable animal-based indicator of compromised welfare.4)
/E (2. Flooring: Proper flooring is essential for maintaining hygiene and preventing injuries and disease in dairy cattle. The Central Pollution Control Board \(CPCB\) guidelines mandate that floors in dairy housing should be impervious, non-slippery, and equipped with a wastewater collection system. Inadequate flooring such as damp, uneven, or abrasive surfaces can lead to respiratory illness in calves and significantly increase the risk of lameness in adult cattle. In India, lameness affects an estimated 8% to 30.5% of dairy cattle and is widely recognised as the most reliable animal-based indicator of compromised welfare.4)
/Pg 22 0 R
/K [5 6 7]
>>
