/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (3. Spurious Oxytocin: The widespread and indiscriminate use of spurious Oxytocin, a Schedule H1 drug, to induce milk letdown in dairy animals has led to serious health issues including mastitis, abortions, delayed puberty, dystocia, and reproductive disorders such as ovarian cysts and anestrous. Its use violates Section 12 of the PCA Act, 1960, and is a cognizable offence. As per Rule 9 of the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals \(Registration of Cattle Premises\) Rules, 1978, Section 12 must also be prominently displayed in the local language at cattle premises to ensure compliance and deter misuse of spurious Oxytocin. )
/E (3. Spurious Oxytocin: The widespread and indiscriminate use of spurious Oxytocin, a Schedule H1 drug, to induce milk letdown in dairy animals has led to serious health issues including mastitis, abortions, delayed puberty, dystocia, and reproductive disorders such as ovarian cysts and anestrous. Its use violates Section 12 of the PCA Act, 1960, and is a cognizable offence. As per Rule 9 of the Prevention of Cruelty to Animals \(Registration of Cattle Premises\) Rules, 1978, Section 12 must also be prominently displayed in the local language at cattle premises to ensure compliance and deter misuse of spurious Oxytocin. )
/Pg 23 0 R
/K [0 1 2]
