<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H1
/T (8. Feed Storage: It is a common practice to feed moldy domestic waste, fodder, and improperly stored feed to the lead to the cattle. However, Section 11\(1\) \(f\) of the PCA Act, requires cattle owners to cattle nutritious food. Additionally, the CPCB Guideline No.3.3 \(iv\) requires the feed given to be of good quality to reduce the enteric methane generation and to improve the quality of life of the cattle. Poor storage leads to mycotoxin contamination, especially Aflatoxin from Aspergillus flavus, which harms cattle and contaminates milk with carcinogenic toxins, posing human health risks. A study in Greater Bengaluru found widespread use of lake fodder contaminated with toxic heavy metals, highlighting the need for feed quality monitoring and secure storage to protect animal welfare and food safety to protect cattle health and ensure sustainable dairy production.14)
/E (8. Feed Storage: It is a common practice to feed moldy domestic waste, fodder, and improperly stored feed to the lead to the cattle. However, Section 11\(1\) \(f\) of the PCA Act, requires cattle owners to cattle nutritious food. Additionally, the CPCB Guideline No.3.3 \(iv\) requires the feed given to be of good quality to reduce the enteric methane generation and to improve the quality of life of the cattle. Poor storage leads to mycotoxin contamination, especially Aflatoxin from Aspergillus flavus, which harms cattle and contaminates milk with carcinogenic toxins, posing human health risks. A study in Greater Bengaluru found widespread use of lake fodder contaminated with toxic heavy metals, highlighting the need for feed quality monitoring and secure storage to protect animal welfare and food safety to protect cattle health and ensure sustainable dairy production.14)
