/E (2. Greenhouse Gas \(GHG\) Emissions: Dairy farms are significant sources of anthropogenic GHG emissions. CPCB Guideline 3.3 mandates proper ventilation in animal housing to ensure fresh air circulation, reducing humidity and preventing the buildup of methane, carbon dioxide, and ammonia. Farms must also take measures to restrict pest access to stored dung to minimize odor. Improving feed quality and supplement dosage can reduce enteric methane emissions, benefiting both animal health and the environment. Additionally, planting trees or establishing green belts around dairy units helps control odors and noise pollution. These steps enhance environmental sustainability and animal welfare. The key GHG emissions from dairy farms include:17)
/Pg 28 0 R
/K [0 1 2 3]
